(text "NAND gates consume less power in real silicon applications - Compared with using NOR gates" (rect 120 56 662 69)(font "DejaVu Sans Condensed" (font_size 8)))
(text "While using a DEMUX to selectively route the clock signal (called Clock Gating) sounds efficient " (rect 96 -8 652 5)(font "DejaVu Sans Condensed" (font_size 8)))
(text "on paper, routing a clock through combinational logic like a DEMUX introduces severe timing hazards in real hardware." (rect 56 8 743 21)(font "DejaVu Sans Condensed" (font_size 8)))
(text "Why clk at the bit level vs using it with DEMX:" (rect 72 -32 339 -19)(font "DejaVu Sans Condensed" (font_size 8)))
